# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>
#
# Types:
#   feat:     A new feature (bumps MINOR version)
#   fix:      A bug fix (bumps PATCH version)
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Formatting, missing semicolons, etc; no code change
#   refactor: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     A code change that improves performance (bumps PATCH version)
#   test:     Adding missing or correcting existing tests
#   build:    Changes to the build system or dependencies
#   ci:       Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
#   chore:    Other changes that don't modify src or test files
#   revert:   Reverts a previous commit
#
# Scope (optional): component affected (e.g., docker, logging, ci)
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Add "BREAKING CHANGE:" in the footer, or append "!" after the type
#   e.g., feat!: remove legacy API
#   This bumps the MAJOR version.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(docker): add health check endpoint
#   fix: resolve startup crash on missing config
#   feat!: drop support for .NET 8
#   docs: update README with build instructions
#   ci: switch to semantic-release
